WEBVTT

00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:03.875
A patient sits down across from
a medical student and says:

00:00:03.875 --> 00:00:05.377
pet mein gola ho raha hai.

00:00:05.844 --> 00:00:09.856
Word for word, something like "a
ball is forming in my stomach".

00:00:09.856 --> 00:00:14.870
It is an everyday way of voicing a
gastrointestinal concern, and it does not map

00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.939
neatly onto any one medical term.

00:00:17.406 --> 00:00:21.901
Picture three students hearing it.
The first writes down "diarrhea".

00:00:21.901 --> 00:00:25.669
The second jumps straight to
a diagnosis. The third asks:

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:28.247
what do you mean by that? Tell me more.

00:00:28.714 --> 00:00:32.645
Only the third has practised
the skill this paper is about.

00:00:32.645 --> 00:00:37.976
The phrase has to be clarified, not mapped
straight to a symptom or a diagnosis.

00:00:38.443 --> 00:00:43.849
The paper proposes a practice copilot:
virtual patients that let trainees in Indian

00:00:43.849 --> 00:00:48.799
medical education rehearse moments like
this, and a way to tell whether they

00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:49.646
actually did.

00:00:50.113 --> 00:00:56.722
It is a design paper. It specifies an
architecture and an evaluation plan, and it

00:00:56.722 --> 00:00:59.007
reports no learner outcomes.

00:01:00.476 --> 00:01:03.281
A clinical encounter is
a chain of decisions:

00:01:03.281 --> 00:01:08.391
what to ask, what to examine, which
information changes the differential, and what

00:01:08.391 --> 00:01:09.077
to do next.

00:01:09.544 --> 00:01:14.625
Clinical reasoning connects a representation
of the problem with organized clinical

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:19.646
knowledge. And management adds choices
under uncertainty, with trade-offs specific

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:20.564
to the patient.

00:01:21.031 --> 00:01:25.567
Now imagine two students who both
arrive at the right diagnosis.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:28.968
One got there by asking,
examining and revising.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.669
The other guessed early.

00:01:31.137 --> 00:01:35.523
The label at the end is identical.
The reasoning behind it is not.

00:01:35.523 --> 00:01:40.241
Correctly naming a diagnosis cannot,
by itself, establish either skill.

00:01:41.709 --> 00:01:46.852
Virtual patients promise repeated, low-stakes
rehearsal of consequential skills, as

00:01:46.852 --> 00:01:48.587
often as a trainee needs it.

00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:54.926
And an expressive patient, one that speaks,
hesitates and uses everyday language,

00:01:54.926 --> 00:01:56.955
could broaden that practice.

00:01:57.422 --> 00:02:02.111
But two things can go wrong. The
first is uncontrolled disclosure:

00:02:02.111 --> 00:02:08.008
a model playing the patient can volunteer
facts nobody asked for, or contradict the

00:02:08.008 --> 00:02:08.363
case.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:13.923
The second is unreliable scoring. A recent
study of a voice-based virtual patient

00:02:13.923 --> 00:02:19.016
found automated communication scores agreed
less with faculty ratings than scores

00:02:19.016 --> 00:02:20.651
for information gathering.

00:02:21.118 --> 00:02:25.093
Either failure can make an
encounter educationally misleading.

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:31.240
Nor are virtual patients new. Earlier work
used them to teach empathy, and EQClinic

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:35.140
gave automated nonverbal
feedback in telehealth training.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:40.410
So the contribution cannot be "we added
an avatar" or "we added communication

00:02:40.410 --> 00:02:41.094
feedback".

00:02:41.561 --> 00:02:46.424
The contribution is a contract: control
what the patient may say, and keep a record

00:02:46.424 --> 00:02:48.826
of what the learner actually did with it.

00:02:50.296 --> 00:02:54.907
The central move is to split the
simulated patient into four layers.

00:02:55.375 --> 00:03:01.288
At the bottom is clinical truth: what is
actually going on, as approved by faculty.

00:03:01.754 --> 00:03:06.867
Above it is patient knowledge: what this
patient understands, remembers and worries

00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:10.193
about, which can be much less
than the clinical truth.

00:03:10.661 --> 00:03:15.917
Then disclosure: which of those facts are
allowed out right now, given what has been

00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:16.730
asked so far.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:22.648
And last, speech realization: how the
permitted facts are actually spoken, in a

00:03:22.648 --> 00:03:24.926
voice, a register and a language.

00:03:25.393 --> 00:03:30.805
The bottom layer is locked. Clinical truth
is not writable through conversation.

00:03:30.805 --> 00:03:35.406
By design, nothing a learner says
should be able to change the case.

00:03:35.874 --> 00:03:40.796
Each case is an immutable version, and a
clinician reviews it before it is used in a

00:03:40.796 --> 00:03:41.440
curriculum.

00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:44.550
Let us make that precise.

00:03:45.017 --> 00:03:49.077
C is the approved case version,
the locked clinical truth.

00:03:49.825 --> 00:03:53.349
K sub t is what the
patient knows at time t.

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:58.395
D sub t is the disclosure state:
what has been revealed so far.

00:03:58.395 --> 00:04:01.359
And H sub t is the encounter history.

00:04:02.106 --> 00:04:07.349
On the learner's side, an interpreter
turns what the student said into a typed

00:04:07.349 --> 00:04:11.852
action, a sub t. For example: ask
what the patient means by "gola".

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:19.705
A policy, pi, takes all five and returns
F sub t, the content the patient is

00:04:19.705 --> 00:04:27.278
permitted to say. F sub t equals pi of C,
K sub t, D sub t, H sub t, and a sub t.

00:04:28.026 --> 00:04:32.823
Here is the boundary that matters. The
speech realizer, the part that actually

00:04:32.823 --> 00:04:36.328
talks, receives only F sub t
and the persona constraints.

00:04:36.328 --> 00:04:38.665
Not the full case, and not the rubric.

00:04:39.132 --> 00:04:44.551
So the voice can be expressive, but it is
never handed the diagnosis to give away.

00:04:45.019 --> 00:04:49.034
One turn, end to end. The student
asks a clarifying question.

00:04:49.034 --> 00:04:54.365
The interpreter types it. The policy checks
the case and what has been disclosed,

00:04:54.365 --> 00:04:59.762
and releases a permitted fact. The realizer
speaks it, and the history updates for

00:04:59.762 --> 00:05:00.683
the next turn.

00:05:01.150 --> 00:05:04.405
Examinations and tests
follow the same discipline.

00:05:04.405 --> 00:05:09.873
Separate services return only findings that
exist in the case, or say plainly that a

00:05:09.873 --> 00:05:12.803
result is unavailable
or needs clarification.

00:05:12.803 --> 00:05:18.271
And asking for an examination is recorded
as a request, not as proof the student can

00:05:18.271 --> 00:05:18.987
perform it.

00:05:20.456 --> 00:05:26.077
Now the assessment side. The paper's
key distinction is between an authored

00:05:26.077 --> 00:05:29.675
opportunity and a demonstrated
learner response.

00:05:30.142 --> 00:05:35.286
For every opportunity that can be
assessed, the system records a tuple, o.

00:05:36.034 --> 00:05:40.489
c identifies the authored
cue. v is its case version.

00:05:40.489 --> 00:05:46.121
m is the modality, such as text or
audio. d is the delivered event.

00:05:46.121 --> 00:05:50.493
w is the response window.
r is the rubric criterion.

00:05:50.493 --> 00:05:56.209
And u is the uncertainty about
whether the cue was really available.

00:05:56.957 --> 00:05:59.706
Why so much bookkeeping?
Consider barge-in.

00:05:59.706 --> 00:06:03.287
The patient is mid-sentence,
and the student interrupts.

00:06:03.287 --> 00:06:06.036
The rest of the queued
speech is cancelled.

00:06:06.503 --> 00:06:11.417
Suppose a cue sat in that cancelled
audio. It was planned, but never played.

00:06:11.417 --> 00:06:16.718
The record separates planned from delivered
content, so that cue cannot be counted

00:06:16.718 --> 00:06:21.567
as heard, and a missed opportunity there
is not scored against the student.

00:06:22.034 --> 00:06:25.084
Even delivered audio is
not automatically enough.

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:28.569
An intended tone does not
prove the cue was perceptible.

00:06:28.569 --> 00:06:33.424
Native-speaker review and playback checks
must establish that before a miss is

00:06:33.424 --> 00:06:33.860
scored.

00:06:34.326 --> 00:06:37.410
Once a cue is delivered,
the record follows a chain:

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:42.154
the student's follow-up, the patient's
clarification, and what the student later

00:06:42.154 --> 00:06:44.941
does with it. Each is
kept as a separate event.

00:06:45.408 --> 00:06:50.540
The paper calls a small clue with this
kind of depth a diagnostic kernel.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:55.672
The rubric can tell apart noticing it,
characterizing it, and using it in

00:06:55.672 --> 00:06:56.445
management.

00:06:56.913 --> 00:07:02.102
Take weight change. A student who asks about
it and then ignores the answer has done

00:07:02.102 --> 00:07:06.859
something different from one who asks
and updates the problem representation.

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:09.515
A keyword count would
credit both the same.

00:07:10.983 --> 00:07:15.168
Patient speech runs on its own
lane, independent of assessment.

00:07:15.635 --> 00:07:20.720
Beside it, asynchronous observers watch
finalized events and propose evidence

00:07:20.720 --> 00:07:26.069
claims, each citing the events behind it.
When the evidence is insufficient, they

00:07:26.069 --> 00:07:26.597
abstain.

00:07:27.063 --> 00:07:30.012
A later scoring stage
reconciles those claims.

00:07:30.012 --> 00:07:35.332
Deterministic rules check approved critical
actions, semantic judgments need review

00:07:35.332 --> 00:07:40.204
against expert labels, and no overall
model grade is treated as a competency

00:07:40.204 --> 00:07:40.781
estimate.

00:07:41.248 --> 00:07:44.139
And failures degrade
instead of corrupting.

00:07:44.139 --> 00:07:48.912
If an observer fails, the event stream
is still there for later review.

00:07:48.912 --> 00:07:54.357
If speech fails, the encounter can fall
back to text, but criteria that depend on

00:07:54.357 --> 00:07:56.105
audio become unassessable.

00:07:57.574 --> 00:08:01.721
Now the learning design. It
starts with supported rehearsal.

00:08:01.721 --> 00:08:07.180
In teaching mode, the learner can ask for
a broad prompt, a specific hint, or a

00:08:07.180 --> 00:08:08.217
worked example.

00:08:08.685 --> 00:08:13.191
Every bit of help is logged, because
assisted performance is not independent

00:08:13.191 --> 00:08:13.903
performance.

00:08:14.371 --> 00:08:19.915
Feedback then highlights a few consequential
moments and supplies a next exercise.

00:08:19.915 --> 00:08:24.310
The next case changes the surface
features and removes the hints.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:28.907
Spaced reassessment comes back later,
and the real test is transfer.

00:08:29.374 --> 00:08:33.868
Here is how that might look. These
screens are a design mock-up filled with

00:08:33.868 --> 00:08:36.924
synthetic data. No learner
has used this interface.

00:08:37.391 --> 00:08:42.682
During a station, a cue bar shows which
authored cues were explored, partly explored

00:08:42.682 --> 00:08:47.847
or missed, quoting the patient's words
without revealing facts nobody asked about.

00:08:48.315 --> 00:08:53.638
After the station, a debrief bands each
rubric domain as strong, developing or

00:08:53.638 --> 00:08:57.391
needing work, each linked to
the turn that supports it.

00:08:57.858 --> 00:09:02.583
Domains that need work become short
drills scheduled at expanding intervals.

00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:07.184
A passing repetition lengthens the
interval, and a failed one shortens it.

00:09:07.651 --> 00:09:13.150
Badges reward practice habits such as
safety-netting, and there is no leaderboard.

00:09:13.150 --> 00:09:18.380
Whether faster feedback and spaced drills
improve independent performance is a

00:09:18.380 --> 00:09:21.599
hypothesis for the learning
study, not a result.

00:09:22.067 --> 00:09:27.237
One more rule: credit follows the learner's
actions, not the patient's reaction.

00:09:27.237 --> 00:09:32.473
A patient's agreement, emotional relief
or compliance is not required for credit.

00:09:32.473 --> 00:09:37.902
Acknowledging uncertainty, respecting
preferences and seeking supervision can all be

00:09:37.902 --> 00:09:39.065
competent actions.

00:09:39.532 --> 00:09:42.406
Why separate help from
learning so carefully?

00:09:42.406 --> 00:09:47.196
A mathematics study distinguishes
supported performance from learning after

00:09:47.196 --> 00:09:52.241
assistance is removed. And in a
diagnostic-reasoning trial, giving physicians a

00:09:52.241 --> 00:09:57.031
language model brought no significant
benefit, despite the model's stronger

00:09:57.031 --> 00:10:02.012
standalone performance. Model competence
and learner development need separate

00:10:02.012 --> 00:10:02.651
endpoints.

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:09.401
How would anyone know whether this works?
The paper specifies four kinds of test.

00:10:09.869 --> 00:10:15.229
First, simulation consistency. Probe
approved cases with paraphrased questions,

00:10:15.229 --> 00:10:20.317
withheld information, incompatible
orders and injection attempts, and count

00:10:20.317 --> 00:10:24.794
contradictions, unauthorized
disclosures and unsupported findings.

00:10:24.794 --> 00:10:27.915
A boundary violation
blocks that case version.

00:10:28.382 --> 00:10:34.721
Second, matched conditions: expressive
audio, neutral audio and text, with the same

00:10:34.721 --> 00:10:39.990
clinical facts. Neutral controls
measure false emotional attribution.

00:10:40.457 --> 00:10:45.813
Third, scoring agreement. Clinicians and
native speakers annotate opportunities

00:10:45.813 --> 00:10:51.305
before seeing automated scores, and agreement
is reported with absolute-agreement

00:10:51.305 --> 00:10:55.576
ICC for continuous ratings and
weighted kappa for ordinal ones.

00:10:56.043 --> 00:11:01.760
Fourth, learning. Usual case practice is
compared with copilot practice, matched for

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:06.933
time and feedback access. The primary
endpoint is a blinded rating of a new,

00:11:06.933 --> 00:11:10.200
unassisted encounter after
a prespecified delay.

00:11:10.668 --> 00:11:14.448
The paper also names its
failure criteria in advance:

00:11:14.448 --> 00:11:20.083
unavailable cues scored as missed,
hallucinated evidence producing remediation,

00:11:20.083 --> 00:11:26.074
systematic penalties tied to a language, or
improvement confined to rehearsed cases.

00:11:26.541 --> 00:11:31.971
If expert agreement or evidence attribution
is inadequate for a scoring dimension,

00:11:31.971 --> 00:11:37.268
that dimension is removed. And if expressive
audio adds no benefit, a successful

00:11:37.268 --> 00:11:39.255
control design is kept anyway.

00:11:40.722 --> 00:11:42.932
So, what this paper does not claim.

00:11:43.400 --> 00:11:48.468
It reports no learner outcomes, no
validated scores and no calibrated mastery

00:11:48.468 --> 00:11:53.405
threshold. Live testing is described
as ongoing, and no results from it are

00:11:53.405 --> 00:11:53.997
reported.

00:11:54.464 --> 00:12:00.569
Hindi, Haryanvi, Bengali, Odia and code-mixed
speech are evaluation targets, not

00:12:00.569 --> 00:12:06.444
validated capabilities. The personas are
constructed examples, not population

00:12:06.444 --> 00:12:10.870
estimates. And every interface
screen uses synthetic data.

00:12:11.337 --> 00:12:16.517
What it does offer is a testable claim:
preserving the link between a presented

00:12:16.517 --> 00:12:21.238
opportunity, the learner's action and
the feedback makes simulation more

00:12:21.238 --> 00:12:23.140
interpretable and assessable.

00:12:23.607 --> 00:12:27.631
Whether that structure improves independent
clinical reasoning and communication

00:12:27.631 --> 00:12:29.190
will need prospective evidence.

00:12:29.657 --> 00:12:33.218
So, back to our patient.
Pet mein gola ho raha hai.

00:12:33.218 --> 00:12:36.570
The response worth practising
was never a guess.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:37.827
It was a question.
